-- title:
--   Infinitesimal Hopf algebras over a perfect field are truncated polynomial algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a perfect field of characteristic $p$ for a prime $p$, and let $H$ be a commutative ring equipped with the structure of a Hopf algebra over $k$ which is finite as a $k$-module. Assume that every $x \in H$ annihilated by the counit of the coalgebra structure is nilpotent, i.e. the augmentation ideal of $H$ is a nil ideal. The conclusion asserts the existence of a natural number $d$ and a family of natural numbers $e : \mathrm{Fin}\, d \to \mathbb{N}$ such that there is a $k$-algebra isomorphism between $H$ and the quotient of the polynomial algebra $k[X_i : i \in \mathrm{Fin}\, d]$ in $d$ variables by the ideal generated by the set of elements $X_i^{p^{e(i)+1}}$, $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\, d$; the isomorphism is produced as the nonemptiness of the type of such algebra equivalences rather than as a specified map. No restriction (such as positivity) is imposed on the exponents $e(i)$ beyond their being natural numbers, so each truncation exponent is a power $p^{e(i)+1} \ge p$.
--
--   This is the classical structure theorem for the coordinate ring of a finite infinitesimal (connected) commutative group scheme over a perfect field of characteristic $p$: its Hopf algebra is a truncated polynomial algebra $k[T_1,\dots,T_d]/(T_1^{p^{e_1+1}},\dots,T_d^{p^{e_d+1}})$. It is used to compute the $k$-dimension of such Hopf algebras as a product of powers of $p$, and in the local case to obtain the corresponding presentation for Hopf algebras over a perfect field whose underlying ring is local.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_exists_algEquiv_mvPolynomial_quotient_X_pow_of_isNilpotent.lean

